{
  "version": 4,
  "_comment": [
    "GENERATED by backend/scripts/gen_grant_profile.py \u2014 do not hand-edit.",
    "",
    "Grouped-privilege profile shared by every writer of Ranger policies: the platform",
    "(UI/CLI/API/MCP) and SQE's SQL GRANT. Two independent transcriptions of these",
    "semantics already drifted -- SQE's WRITE_ACCESS carried table-properties-write,",
    "which table-data-write does NOT imply -- so the definition lives here once.",
    "",
    "seeds are expanded transitively through impliedGrants from servicedef-polaris.json",
    "(Ranger is the source of truth for what an access type means; Polaris's embedded",
    "authorizer does not apply impliedGrants itself, so a writer must expand them before",
    "writing the policy). `exclude` is subtracted AFTER expansion.",
    "",
    "level picks which keys go in the Ranger resource map. A privilege spans SEVERAL",
    "levels on purpose: reading one table needs catalog-level namespace-list, because",
    "Polaris resolves the catalog before it looks at the table. Writing only the deepest",
    "level produces a policy the engine can never reach.",
    "",
    "INSERT vs MODIFY: both seed table-data-write, but INSERT excludes table-location-set,",
    "table-uuid-assign and table-format-version-upgrade -- otherwise an append-only",
    "pipeline role could REPOINT the table at different storage. Snowflake separates",
    "INSERT from ALTER for the same reason.",
    "",
    "fixtures are the cross-writer contract. Both repos run them; if SQE and the platform",
    "disagree on one byte, a test fails instead of a deployment behaving differently",
    "depending on which surface issued the grant.",
    "",
    "rejects (v3) are inputs every writer must REFUSE. A privilege whose plan stops above",
    "the requested coordinate used to have that coordinate silently dropped -- MANAGE on",
    "wh.sales.orders wrote a CATALOG-WIDE policy and echoed the narrow scope back as if it",
    "had been honoured -- so a ws-admin granting one table handed over the whole catalog.",
    "Only that direction is a defect: a request shallower than the plan is fine (see the",
    "level-truncation fixtures). A fully-wildcard coordinate (*) is not a rejection."
  ],
